course: dictionary
lesson: 13747
title: Used interchangeably
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Interchangeably is a long word, but you can spot its parts. Change is in the middle, and -ably tells you it describes how something is done. So it is about how things can be changed or swapped.
explain: «In this room, sofa and couch can be used interchangeably.» You can say sofa or couch and the meaning stays the same. Try the swap test: «The cat sat on the couch» becomes «The cat sat on the sofa». It still makes sense, and it means the same thing.
explain: Not every pair can be swapped. «Cat and dog cannot be used interchangeably, because a cat is not a dog.» If swapping changes the meaning, the words are not interchangeable. In maths, «3 + 4» and «4 + 3» can be used interchangeably, because they give the same answer.
fact: Interchangeably is an adverb, so it tells you how things can be swapped.
fact: Two or more things can be used interchangeably when you can swap them without changing the result or meaning.
fact: The swap test helps: put one word in place of the other and check that the meaning stays the same.
fact: «Sofa» and «couch» are used interchangeably in many homes.
fact: The same idea appears in science and maths, where parts or numbers can fit each other in either order and still work.
exercise: «The words sofa and couch are used interchangeably in this book.» What does interchangeably mean here? | They are always used in a race | They must never be used together | They are the same word spelled two ways | *They can be swapped and mean the same thing
exercise: Which pair of words can be used interchangeably? | hot and fork | *big and large | cat and dog | red and table
exercise: Ella says «3 + 4» and «4 + 3» can be used interchangeably. Is she right? | No, because one is bigger | Only on Tuesdays | No, the answers are different | *Yes, they give the same answer
test: Which pair could be used interchangeably in a sentence? | hat and shoe | *start and begin | cup and bed | run and sleep
test: Which phrase means the same as "can be swapped for each other without changing the meaning"? | used in a hurry | used separately | never used | *used interchangeably
exam: Which sentence is the best example of interchangeably? | The sun is very bright today | She ran to the shop quickly | The bus was late, so we walked | *Sofa and couch can be used interchangeably in this room
